From 58528b6470a6eccad9c8a3542275fb2d06fa079c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:56:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] feat(train): leave depth features out when training on
 RGB-D datasets

No policy Studio trains takes depth maps: ACT, SmolVLA, Pi05 and MolmoAct2
crash on a 1-channel image, XR0 and RLDX1 clamp millimetres to [0, 1].
LeRobotDataModule and its dataset adapter get exclude_depth, which drops the
depth features from the loaded metadata (in memory only), so samples no
longer decode them. Studio passes it when the dataset has depth features.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
